  "$comment": "Map cities and markets (D28, D44; contracts enums.ts MetroId and MarketId). Names, /search query strings and public coordinates only (D29): locality ids are resolved at runtime and pinned in the database, never stored here. gazetteer: the 13 map cities, each with neighbourhood polygons (LIFT, BLOCK, areas) in packages/geo and its boundary source; its bbox is the gazetteer's bounds rounded outward to two decimals. markets: the 51 market ids for locality contexts (SHARE metros, SLATE markets, RANK metro contexts), major markets first; every map city is also a market with the same names, centre and bbox. Place search runs around a market's centre (a map city's METRO_CENTRES point) with a radius that reaches the farthest corner of its bbox, at least 25 miles (D44). query and state_name narrow the /search for a locality; they do not always disambiguate it. query uses the spelling the locality search knows where it differs from the label: St. Louis is searched as Saint Louis. pin: deliberate marks a name whose locality a person chooses and pins in kv, never picked automatically: Austin (the probe sweep found two exact localities in Texas) and Washington (the name also matches the state). Destination search returns no state for these names, so destination ids need their own resolution path. Coordinates use two decimals; bbox is lon/lat degrees.",
